          <h3>01 — Initial consultation</h3>
          <p>A 30-to-60-minute call with an engineer, not a salesperson. We discuss your goals, timeline, constraints, and current environment. We ask technical questions about your network topology, existing vendors, security posture, and regulatory requirements, then listen carefully before responding. We tell you honestly whether we are the right partner for the engagement — and if we are not, we will point you to someone who is. You will leave this call with a clear picture of next steps, even if those steps do not involve MEAICON.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-card">
          <div class="feature-icon"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M11.42 15.17L17.25 21A2.652 2.652 0 0021 17.25l-5.877-5.877M11.42 15.17l-2.51-5.31M11.42 15.17l-5.31 2.51"/></svg></div>
          <h3>02 — Technical assessment</h3>
          <p>If there is a fit, we conduct a structured assessment of your current infrastructure — network topology, security posture, data centre capacity, and operational gaps. We review documentation, run non-intrusive discovery scans with your approval, and interview your in-house engineers to understand what works and what does not. The output is a documented baseline with prioritised risks, costed remediation options, and a recommended target architecture — delivered as a written report you own, not a slide deck you forget.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-card">
          <div class="feature-icon"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m5.618-4.016A11.955 11.955 0 0112 2.944a11.955 11.955 0 01-8.618 3.04A12.02 12.02 0 003 9c0 5.591 3.824 10.29 9 11.622 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.462-.249-2.84-.685-4.016"/></svg></div>
          <h3>03 — Proposal &amp; SOW</h3>
          <p>You receive a structured proposal with architecture diagrams, scope, bill of quantities, implementation timeline, budget, and an operational handover plan — signed off by our engineering team, not generated by a template. The accompanying statement of work defines deliverables, acceptance criteria, SLA commitments, and change-management procedures so there is no ambiguity during execution. You decide what to proceed with, on your timeline, with full visibility into what you are buying and why.</p>
        </article>
